# DNA-AND content · life · animals (domain Eukaryotes, kingdom Animalia)
# researched: Pearson "Animal diversity, body plans, phylogeny"; Wikibooks General Biology "Animal Evolution";
#   Wikipedia "List of insect orders"; NCSU insect orders; MSU 2016 insect-order classification;
#   standard zoology for mammal, bird, reptile, amphibian and fish groups
# Animals have about 35 phyla. The main ones are here; orders below each class fill to 100 in play.
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · wiki/systems/r08-life-sim.md · docs/wiki/tree-of-life.md

# ── Body-plan traits ──

@trait no-symmetry
name: No symmetry
real: yes
example: sponges, placozoans

@trait radial
name: Radial symmetry
real: yes
says: a round body with parts arranged around a center
example: jellyfish, corals

@trait bilateral
name: Bilateral symmetry
real: yes
says: a left and right side, a front and back, a head end

@trait two-layers
name: Two tissue layers
real: yes
example: jellyfish, comb jellies

@trait three-layers
name: Three tissue layers
real: yes
says: allows muscles and organs

@trait solid-body
name: No body cavity
real: yes
example: flatworms

@trait false-cavity
name: Partial body cavity
real: yes
example: roundworms, rotifers

@trait true-cavity
name: True body cavity
real: yes
example: mollusks, arthropods, echinoderms, chordates

@trait segments
name: Segmented body
real: yes
example: earthworms, insects, vertebrate spines

@trait molting
name: Molting
real: yes
says: sheds its outer skin to grow (the molting branch: roundworms, arthropods, water bears)

@trait mouth-first
name: Mouth-first development
real: yes
says: the first opening in the embryo becomes the mouth (protostomes)

@trait anus-first
name: Anus-first development
real: yes
says: the first opening becomes the anus (deuterostomes: echinoderms, chordates)

# ── Phyla ──

@phylum sponges
name: Sponges (Porifera)
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: no tissues, no symmetry; filter water through their pores

@phylum placozoans
name: Placozoans
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: tiny flat crawling sheets of cells, the simplest animals

@phylum comb-jellies
name: Comb jellies (Ctenophora)
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: swim with rows of beating combs that shimmer

@phylum cnidarians
name: Cnidarians
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: jellyfish, corals, anemones; stinging cells; polyp and medusa forms

@phylum flatworms
name: Flatworms (Platyhelminthes)
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: flat, solid-bodied worms; many parasites

@phylum rotifers
name: Rotifers
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: microscopic animals with a spinning crown of hairs

@phylum roundworms
name: Roundworms (Nematoda)
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: tiny worms in soil, water and bodies everywhere

@phylum segmented-worms
name: Segmented worms (Annelida)
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: earthworms, leeches, bristle worms

@phylum mollusks
name: Mollusks
real: yes
kingdom: animals
classes: snails and slugs, clams and oysters, octopuses and squid, chitons

@phylum arthropods
name: Arthropods
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: jointed legs and a hard outer skeleton; the largest phylum
classes: insects, arachnids, crustaceans, myriapods

@phylum water-bears
name: Water bears (Tardigrada)
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: tiny eight-legged animals that survive boiling, freezing, drying and space

@phylum velvet-worms
name: Velvet worms (Onychophora)
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: soft walking worms that shoot glue at prey

@phylum moss-animals
name: Moss animals (Bryozoa)
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: tiny colonies that filter food with a ring of tentacles

@phylum lamp-shells
name: Lamp shells (Brachiopoda)
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: shelled filter feeders, ancient and once everywhere

@phylum echinoderms
name: Echinoderms
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: starfish, urchins, sea cucumbers; five-part bodies and water-powered tube feet

@phylum acorn-worms
name: Acorn worms (Hemichordata)
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: worm-like relatives of chordates

@phylum chordates
name: Chordates
real: yes
kingdom: animals
says: a nerve cord down the back; includes all animals with backbones

# ── Arthropod classes ──

@class insects
name: Insects
real: yes
phylum: arthropods
says: six legs, three body parts; most kinds of animal on Earth are insects

@class arachnids
name: Arachnids
real: yes
phylum: arthropods
says: eight legs: spiders, scorpions, mites, ticks

@class crustaceans
name: Crustaceans
real: yes
phylum: arthropods
says: crabs, lobsters, shrimp, krill, woodlice

@class myriapods
name: Myriapods
real: yes
phylum: arthropods
says: centipedes and millipedes

# ── Insect orders (seeds) ──

@order beetles
name: Beetles (Coleoptera)
real: yes
class: insects
says: the biggest order of all

@order bees-wasps-ants
name: Bees, wasps and ants (Hymenoptera)
real: yes
class: insects
says: home of most hive and colony life

@order butterflies-moths
name: Butterflies and moths (Lepidoptera)
real: yes
class: insects

@order flies
name: Flies (Diptera)
real: yes
class: insects
says: flies and mosquitoes; two wings

@order true-bugs
name: True bugs (Hemiptera)
real: yes
class: insects
says: sucking mouthparts: cicadas, aphids, stink bugs

@order grasshoppers
name: Grasshoppers and crickets (Orthoptera)
real: yes
class: insects

@order dragonflies
name: Dragonflies and damselflies (Odonata)
real: yes
class: insects

@order cockroaches-termites
name: Cockroaches and termites (Blattodea)
real: yes
class: insects
says: termites build huge colonies and mounds

@order mantises
name: Mantises (Mantodea)
real: yes
class: insects

@order stick-insects
name: Stick and leaf insects (Phasmida)
real: yes
class: insects

@order earwigs
name: Earwigs (Dermaptera)
real: yes
class: insects

@order lice
name: Lice
real: yes
class: insects

@order fleas
name: Fleas (Siphonaptera)
real: yes
class: insects

@order mayflies
name: Mayflies (Ephemeroptera)
real: yes
class: insects

@order caddisflies
name: Caddisflies (Trichoptera)
real: yes
class: insects

# ── Fish classes ──

@class hagfish
name: Hagfish
real: yes
phylum: chordates

@class lampreys
name: Lampreys
real: yes
phylum: chordates
says: jawless, sucker-mouthed

@class cartilaginous-fish
name: Cartilaginous fish
real: yes
phylum: chordates
says: sharks, rays, skates, chimaeras; skeletons of cartilage

@class ray-finned-fish
name: Ray-finned fish
real: yes
phylum: chordates
says: almost all fish alive today

@class lobe-finned-fish
name: Lobe-finned fish
real: yes
phylum: chordates
says: coelacanths and lungfish; the line that walked onto land

# ── Land vertebrate classes ──

@class amphibians
name: Amphibians
real: yes
phylum: chordates
orders: frogs and toads, salamanders and newts, caecilians

@class reptiles
name: Reptiles
real: yes
phylum: chordates
orders: lizards and snakes, turtles, crocodiles, tuatara

@class birds
name: Birds
real: yes
phylum: chordates
says: feathered, egg-laying, the living dinosaurs

@class mammals
name: Mammals
real: yes
phylum: chordates
says: hair and milk
subclasses: egg-layers (monotremes), pouched (marsupials), placentals

# ── Bird orders (seeds) ──

@order perching-birds
name: Perching birds (Passeriformes)
real: yes
class: birds
says: more than half of all bird species

@order birds-of-prey
name: Hawks and eagles (Accipitriformes)
real: yes
class: birds

@order falcons
name: Falcons (Falconiformes)
real: yes
class: birds

@order owls
name: Owls (Strigiformes)
real: yes
class: birds

@order parrots
name: Parrots (Psittaciformes)
real: yes
class: birds
says: among the smartest birds

@family corvids
name: Crows, ravens and jays (Corvidae)
real: yes
order: perching-birds
says: among the smartest animals; tool users

@order waterfowl
name: Ducks, geese and swans (Anseriformes)
real: yes
class: birds

@order fowl
name: Chickens and pheasants (Galliformes)
real: yes
class: birds

@order penguins
name: Penguins (Sphenisciformes)
real: yes
class: birds

@order flightless-ratites
name: Ostriches, emus and kiwis
real: yes
class: birds

@order hummingbirds-swifts
name: Hummingbirds and swifts
real: yes
class: birds

@order pigeons
name: Pigeons and doves (Columbiformes)
real: yes
class: birds

# ── Mammal orders (seeds) ──

@order monotremes
name: Egg-laying mammals (Monotremata)
real: yes
class: mammals
example: platypus, echidna

@order marsupials
name: Pouched mammals (marsupials)
real: yes
class: mammals
example: kangaroos, koalas, opossums

@order primates
name: Primates
real: yes
class: mammals
says: lemurs, monkeys, apes, humans

@order rodents
name: Rodents (Rodentia)
real: yes
class: mammals
says: the largest mammal order

@order bats
name: Bats (Chiroptera)
real: yes
class: mammals
says: the only flying mammals

@order carnivores
name: Carnivores (Carnivora)
real: yes
class: mammals
says: cats, dogs and wolves, bears, seals, weasels

@order whales-hoofed
name: Whales and even-toed hoofed mammals (Artiodactyla)
real: yes
class: mammals
says: whales, dolphins, deer, cattle, pigs, hippos

@order odd-toed
name: Odd-toed hoofed mammals (Perissodactyla)
real: yes
class: mammals
says: horses, rhinos, tapirs

@order elephants
name: Elephants (Proboscidea)
real: yes
class: mammals

@order rabbits
name: Rabbits and hares (Lagomorpha)
real: yes
class: mammals

@order insectivores
name: Shrews, moles and hedgehogs (Eulipotyphla)
real: yes
class: mammals

@order sloths-anteaters
name: Sloths and anteaters (Pilosa)
real: yes
class: mammals

@order armadillos
name: Armadillos (Cingulata)
real: yes
class: mammals

@order sea-cows
name: Manatees and dugongs (Sirenia)
real: yes
class: mammals

@order pangolins
name: Pangolins (Pholidota)
real: yes
class: mammals

# ── Generator rules ──

@rule animal-body-plan
real: rule
says: every animal's body comes from its genes: symmetry, layers, body cavity, segments, skeleton, limbs, eyes, skin

@rule animal-tree
real: rule
says: new animals branch from real lines: phylum, then class, order, family, genus, species, each filling to 100 in play with invented ones

@rule animal-convergence
real: rule
says: unrelated lines can evolve the same answer (wings, eyes, fins), because the same problems shape them

@rule animal-intelligence
real: rule
says: any line can climb to intelligence: primates, wolves, crows, parrots, octopuses, whales, social insects (the grouping ladder)

@rule animal-extinction
real: rule
says: lines die out; extinct groups like trilobites and dinosaurs stay greyed out on the tree forever
